'' A BYVAL UDT SETTER VALUE OF THE SAME TYPE is copied as a call's argument is: the copy constructor
'' into a temporary, its address, the destructor after the call. 'o.Q( 1 ) = vv' over a V with a
'' destructor passed the loaded aggregate where the setter takes a pointer, and clang refused the
'' module. A trivial byval W is unchanged; the setter's own changes never reach 'vv'. fbc-modern's output.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/setter-byval-copy.bas -o tests/codegen/setterbyvalcopy.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/setterbyvalcopy.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ctor 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: copy 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: Q 1 7 n7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: R 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: copy 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: S 107
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 107
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: vv 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: end
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 7
